#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:200
msgid "KVM_DEV_ARM_VGIC_GRP_IST"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:202
msgid ""
"This interface is used to either save the state of the IRS's Interrupt State "
"Tables (ISTs), or to restore them. A get operation saves IST state, and a "
"set operation restores IST state. kvm_device_attr.attr is reserved and must "
"be zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:207
msgid ""
"The VGIC must be initialized before using this interface. Restore must be "
"performed before the VM has run. For restore, userspace must have already "
"restored the IRS state needed to describe any guest LPI IST."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:211
msgid ""
"Saving first asks the IRS to save and quiesce the VM so that interrupt state "
"has been written back to the ISTs. KVM checks that the VM remains quiesced "
"while copying out the SPI and LPI IST state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:215
msgid "kvm_device_attr.addr points to a struct kvm_vgic_v5_ist::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:224
msgid ""
"The SPI and LPI IST buffers contain one little-endian 32-bit IST entry per "
"interrupt, in interrupt number order. Only the architected 32-bit ISTE state "
"is exposed to userspace; host IST layout and metadata are private to KVM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:229
msgid "The SPI IST buffer is required and its size must be:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:231
msgid "nr_spis * sizeof(__u32)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:233
msgid ""
"where nr_spis is the value returned by KVM_DEV_ARM_VGIC_GRP_NR_IRQS for the "
"VGICv5 device. For VGICv5 this value is the number of SPIs, not the total "
"number of interrupts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:237
msgid ""
"The LPI IST buffer is required if the guest's IRS_IST_CFGR and IRS_IST_BASER "
"state describes a valid LPI IST, and its size must be:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:240
msgid "BIT(lpi_id_bits) * sizeof(__u32)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:242
msgid ""
"where lpi_id_bits is the LPI ID width configured in IRS_IST_CFGR. If no LPI "
"IST is configured, lpi_ist_addr and lpi_ist_size must both be zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:248
msgid ""
"One or more VCPUs are running, the VGIC is not initialized, restore was "
"requested after the VM has run, an LPI IST already exists, or the save "
"operation completed but the VM did not remain quiesced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../virt/kvm/devices/arm-vgic-v5.rst:252
msgid ""
"attr->addr is NULL, the userspace IST descriptor is missing a required "
"buffer, supplies a non-zero LPI buffer when no LPI IST is configured, has a "
"buffer size that does not match the configured VGICv5 IST state, or an "
"internal VM table operation rejected the VM state"
msgstr ""

